"app container" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		AppContainer
		<header>The box a compiled spell program draws in.</>
	</>

	<text class="lede" paragraph>An empty box the running program draws itself into. The app draws the box once and never touches what's inside it: that belongs to the program.</>
	<list class="spell-meta">
		<item icon="user">Written for: anyone changing how the spell app runs programs</>
		<item icon="image">A picture, not live: the box with Solitaire drawn in it</>
	</>

	<section label="1. What it looks like">
		<icon slot="icon" name="image"/>
		<text paragraph>The editor's App pane without its toolbar, as the editor draws it: the scrolling box, with the Solitaire example filling it.</>
		<image src="/components/app/_images/AppContainer.png" alt="A box filled by a game of Spell Solitaire:  its dark header, then the cards on green" appearance="bordered rounded"/>
		<text class="meta" paragraph>A picture, taken by <text code>yarn site:pictures</> in <link target="src-spell-app" link="/"><text code>spell-app</></>.</>
	</>

	<section label="2. Using it">
		<icon slot="icon" name="code"/>
		<text paragraph>Only <link target="src-packages-app-docs-approot-html" link="/app-root">AppRoot</> draws one, and hands its box to the editor:</>
		<text paragraph>AppRoot.tsx · the program's box:</>
		<markdown>
			```typescript
			<AppContainer
			  scrolling={props.scrolling ?? true}
			  padded={props.padded ?? true}
			  appRef={(element) => {
			    appElement = element
			    editor.setAppRoot(element)
			  }}
			/>
			```
		</>
		<list bulleted>
			<item><text code>appRef</> is told which element the program draws in, once it's on the page.</>
			<item>The program draws with its own Solid root on that element, when it starts: the app's Solid draws the element once and leaves what's inside alone.</>
			<item>The element's id is <text code>spell-app-root</>: where a program draws when no one has said where. The id is written out, not imported, because the app must never load the program's runtime itself.</>
			<item>It imports nothing from the app's other components, so a runner could use it without pulling in the editor. The VS Code runner draws a box with the same class and look, but not this component.</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="3. Props, and where it's drawn">
		<icon slot="icon" name="list check"/>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-api family="AppContainer"></>
		</>
		<text class="meta" paragraph>From its code, by <text code>yarn site:data</> in <link target="src-spell-app" link="/"><text code>spell-app</></>.</>
	</>

	<section label="4. Its code">
		<icon slot="icon" name="folder open"/>
		<list bulleted>
			<item><link target="src-packages-app-src-solid-appcontainer-tsx" link="/src/app/solid/AppContainer.tsx"><text title="src/app/solid/AppContainer.tsx" code>AppContainer.tsx</></>: the component, and its props</>
			<item><link target="src-packages-app-src-solid-appcontainer-css" link="/src/app/solid/AppContainer.css"><text title="src/app/solid/AppContainer.css" code>AppContainer.css</></>: its look, shared with the VS Code runner's box</>
			<item>In the app's Solid components, <text code>app/app/solid</>: <link target="src-packages-app-src-solid" link="/src/app/solid/"><text title="src/app/solid/" code>src/solid/</></></>
		</>
	</>
	<html>
